OL,4,CChef visits schools to share dyslexia  
OL,5,Cexperiences                            
OL,6,GA chef who was diagnosed with dyslexia 
OL,7,Gaged 61 says living with the condition 
OL,8,Gallows him to find "original ways of   
OL,9,Gsolving problems".                     
OL,11,FNick Jaye, from Brighton, retrained as 
OL,12,Fa chef in his late 50s after working   
OL,13,Fas an estate agent and went on to      
OL,14,Fwrite his own recipe book designed to  
OL,15,Fbe read easily by people with dyslexia.
OL,17,FJaye, who says he left school at 15    
OL,18,Fwith no qualifications, has visited    
OL,19,Fspecialist dyslexia school Frewen      
OL,20,FCollege in Rye, and Northiam Primary   
OL,21,FSchool in East Sussex, to share his    
OL,22,Fexperiences.                      G2/4 
